%% SECTION Schedule
@@
Which document defines the scheduling methodology, units of measure, control thresholds and rules of performance measurement?
A) Schedule management plan
B) Schedule baseline
C) Milestone list
D) Activity attributes
= A
? The schedule management plan, created in Plan Schedule Management, sets the rules for developing and controlling the schedule.

@@
What is the duration of a milestone?
A) Zero
B) One day
C) The length of the longest activity
D) It depends on the critical path
= A
? Milestones mark significant points or events and have zero duration.

@@
An activity requires concrete to cure for 7 days before the next activity can start. How is this represented?
A) A lag of 7 days on the finish-to-start relationship
B) A lead of 7 days on the finish-to-start relationship
C) A start-to-finish relationship with a 7-day duration
D) Seven days of free float on the curing activity
= A
? A lag is a required delay between the predecessor and successor.

@@
A team decides to start writing the user manual 5 days before the software is finished. This is an example of:
A) A lead
B) A lag
C) A mandatory dependency
D) Resource levelling
= A
? A lead allows the successor to start before the predecessor finishes.

@@
Network: A (2 days, start), B (4, after A), C (6, after A), D (3, after B), E (2, after C and D). What is the critical path?
A) A-C-E (10 days)
B) A-B-D-E (11 days)
C) A-B-D (9 days)
D) A-C (8 days)
= B
? Path A-B-D-E = 2 + 4 + 3 + 2 = 11 days; path A-C-E = 2 + 6 + 2 = 10 days. The longest path, A-B-D-E, is critical.

@@
In the same network (A 2, B 4 after A, C 6 after A, D 3 after B, E 2 after C and D), what is the total float of activity C?
A) 1 day
B) 0 days
C) 2 days
D) 3 days
= A
? C can start at day 2 and finish at day 8; E starts at day 9 (after D). C's late finish is 9, so its float is 9 − 8 = 1 day.

@@
Two critical-path activities can be shortened. Activity X: 2 days saved for $6,000 total. Activity Y: 2 days saved for $4,000 total. The project needs to save 2 days at the least cost. What should be crashed?
A) Activity Y
B) Activity X
C) Both X and Y
D) A non-critical activity
= A
? Crash the critical activity with the lowest cost per day saved: Y costs $2,000 per day versus $3,000 for X.

@@
Which risk is most associated with fast tracking?
A) Rework, because activities start before their predecessors are complete
B) Higher direct costs, because overtime and extra staff must be paid for the compressed work
C) Lower resource availability for other projects in the portfolio
D) A longer overall duration, because activities wait for each other
= A
? Fast tracking overlaps activities, increasing the risk of rework. Crashing increases cost.

@@
A specialist is assigned to two activities scheduled at the same time. The project manager delays one activity until the specialist is free, extending the project end date. Which technique was used?
A) Resource levelling
B) Resource smoothing
C) Fast tracking
D) Crashing
= A
? Resource levelling resolves over-allocation even if the critical path and end date change. Smoothing stays within float.

@@
Which estimating technique uses historical data and a statistical relationship, such as cost per square metre?
A) Parametric
B) Analogous
C) Bottom-up
D) Expert judgment only
= A
? Parametric estimating multiplies a quantity by a historical unit rate or uses other statistical relationships.

@@
Which estimating technique is generally the most accurate but also the most time-consuming?
A) Bottom-up
B) Analogous
C) Rough order of magnitude
D) Top-down
= A
? Bottom-up estimates each component in detail and aggregates the results.

@@ | fill
Activity estimates: O = 8, M = 11, P = 20 days. What is the triangular (simple average) estimate in days?
= 13
? Triangular estimate = (O + M + P) / 3 = (8 + 11 + 20) / 3 = 39 / 3 = 13 days.

@@
A release burnup chart shows the total-scope line rising every sprint while the completed-work line rises steadily. What is the most likely conclusion?
A) Scope is growing, which may delay the release unless scope is managed
B) The team's velocity is decreasing and the team needs more coaching
C) The team has stopped delivering any completed work during the most recent sprints
D) The project is ahead of schedule because more work is being added
= A
? The rising scope line reveals scope growth; the completed line shows the team continues to deliver.

@@
Which critical chain element protects the project end date from variation along the critical chain?
A) Project buffer
B) Feeding buffer
C) Resource buffer
D) Free float
= A
? The project buffer is placed at the end of the critical chain. Feeding buffers protect where non-critical chains join it.

@@
A Kanban team wants to reduce the time items take to move from "in progress" to "done". What is the most direct lever according to Little's Law?
A) Reduce work in progress
B) Increase the number of columns on the board
C) Start more work at once
D) Estimate items in hours instead of points
= A
? Cycle time equals WIP divided by throughput; reducing WIP reduces cycle time when throughput is stable.

@@
Which chart is most appropriate to show senior executives only the key dates of a project?
A) Milestone chart
B) Detailed network diagram
C) Activity list
D) Resource histogram
= A
? Milestone charts show only major events and are suited for executive audiences.

@@
A project manager plans the next two months in detail and leaves later work as planning packages. This approach is called:
A) Rolling wave planning
B) Critical chain
C) Crashing
D) Fast tracking
= A
? Rolling wave planning details near-term work and elaborates later work progressively.

@@ | multi
Which two statements about free float are correct? (Choose two.)
A) It is the time an activity can be delayed without delaying the early start of any successor
B) It can never be greater than the activity's total float
C) It is always equal to total float
D) It applies only to critical-path activities
E) It is the time the project can be delayed without penalty
= A, B
? Free float concerns successors' early starts and cannot exceed total float, which concerns the project end date.

@@
The team's velocity for the last four sprints was 18, 22, 20 and 20. The remaining backlog for the release is 120 points. How many sprints should be planned?
A) 6
B) 5
C) 7
D) 8
= A
? Average velocity = 80 / 4 = 20 points. 120 / 20 = 6 sprints.

@@
A non-critical activity with 8 days of total float is delayed by 3 days. What is the effect on the project end date?
A) None, as long as the delay stays within the float and nothing else changes
B) The project end date moves by 3 days, as with any delayed activity
C) The project end date moves by 8 days, the full amount of the float
D) The activity becomes critical immediately, and the project end date slips by 3 days
= A
? A delay within total float does not affect the end date, although the remaining float is reduced to 5 days.
